---
title: Element 2: Deadline for Data Sharing
---
sort_key: 2
---
menu: /help/guides/nih
---
body:

#### Question

Will the scientific data underlying peer-reviewed publications be shared by the time of publication, or for other findings, by the end of the period of performance, which includes no-cost extensions?

#### Guidance for Response

A response of "Yes" is expected, unless there are mitigating factors that might push the date of data sharing farther out than the deadlines listed above. These can include student involvement in a research project, or an institution's requirements for certain data files to remain under institutional control for set periods due to patents, licensing, data use agreements, etc. Check with your office of research and/or office of sponsored projects; patent, IP, or inventions office; or legal office if you have questions about the start date for data sharing.

!!! info
    **Zenodo note:** Zenodo offers the ability to embargo deposited files until a date the depositor specifies. Therefore, if you receive institutional permission to make your data files available to the public on a certain date, you can set that date within your deposit record, and the associated files' status will automatically be updated from "Private" to "Public" on that date.

---
